  "note": "The Rhine economy in early 1991: coal and steel in structural decline in the Ruhr, Saar, Wallonia, Lorraine and Luxembourg, chemicals along the Rhine, autos and engineering in the south, banks and insurers in Frankfurt, Luxembourg and the Randstad, state-owned and Treuhand-held industry in the east, and the logistics that tie it together. Every firm keeps its plants in regions that use its own country's money; carriers may pin the lanes they open on across a border, so the Rotterdam and Antwerp pipelines to the Ruhr exist from day one. At least two named firms per industry.",
